  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 247 AM EST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nToday...A stationary front across the FL panhandle will begin to\npush SE today. Ahead of the front moisture increases slightly with\nHRRR and RRFS models showing isolated showers developing first \nacross the Treasure coast counties late this morning into the \nafternoon. Then additional showers develop across northern \nsections later in the day. Brief downpours will be possible in a \nfew areas but accumulations will be less than 0.25\". Warm again \nwith above normal temperatures reaching the mid 80s with light \nwinds, turning onshore up to 10 mph behind the sea breeze. \n\nNon-tropical low pressure east of the Bahamas is sending\nadditional swells toward the FL east coast. Buoy 009 is showing an\nuptick in swell height and period which will produce a High risk\nof rip currents at all central FL Atlc beaches today. This High\nrisk will extend into the weekend and probably early next week.\n\nSat-Thu...The cool front is forecast to cross central Florida \nSaturday. Limited moisture along the boundary itself means it will\nlikely be a dry frontal passage. A wind shift out of the N/NW \nwill announce its passage. Winds gradually veer N/NE Sun and Mon \nas high pressure builds in behind this boundary. GFS and ECMWF are\nin better agreement showing a weaker mid-level S/W trough moving \nacross the deep South, but timing differences remain on when it \ncrosses Florida into next week. The GFS is the faster of the two, \nincreasing rainfall across the area Wednesday with the ECMWF \nholding off better rainfall potential until Wednesday night/ \nThursday. Rain chances for the time being remain out of the \nforecast Sunday with only low rain chances (10-20%) for much of \nthe region Mon-Wed with scattered (30%) showers Thu. Given the \nweakening upper support, severe weather looks unlikely with this \nmid week system. Temperatures trend cooler this weekend behind the\nfront though Sat still looks warm in the low to mid 80s. Near \nnormal highs in the upper 70s/lower 80s Sun-Wed; a little cooler\nThu with more clouds and showers. Min temps forecast in the upper\n50s NW of I-4 next week with 60s elsewhere.",
